{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_90f301d2df04b46464e044e002a198c73437c6e0da55af0e212e1e617fc5df74", "title": "Paul N. J. Ottosson", "text": "Paul N. J. Ottosson (born 25 February 1966) is a Swedish sound designer. He won a total of three Academy Awards. Two for the film \"The Hurt Locker\", one for \"Zero Dark Thirty\", and was nominated for a fourth for \"Spider-Man 2\". He has worked on more than 100 films since 1995.", "score": 47.6117}, {"id": "hp_doc_9d144ae6c9c96a542c76e769dfbe833086e710faec7cb44ccfbb4f6394b8e6ce", "title": "George L. Little", "text": "George L. Little (1950 or 1951 – August 29, 2014) was an American costume designer. He was best known for his work on Kathryn Bigelow's acclaimed war films, \"The Hurt Locker\" and \"Zero Dark Thirty\", the latter of which earned him a nomination from the Costume Designers Guild Awards in the Excellence in Contemporary Film category. He was also nominated for an Emmy Award for his work on the 1988 miniseries \"Lincoln\".", "score": 39.5092}, {"id": "hp_doc_3284ced80ffbe98347c41a87bb7702c971587b4554b3429fdbd7e304a52aff61", "title": "Zero Dark Thirty", "text": "Zero Dark Thirty is a 2012 American political action-thriller film directed by Kathryn Bigelow and written by Mark Boal. Billed as \"the greatest manhunt in history,\" the film dramatizes the nearly decade-long international manhunt for al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden after the September 11 attacks in the United States. This search eventually leads to the discovery of his compound in Pakistan and the military raid that resulted in bin Laden's death on May 2, 2011.", "score": 27.0163}], "remaining_searches": 1}
